A. Level 1 and Level 2.
1. Permitted Locations.
i. Interior parking rows;
ii. Side or rear parking areas;
iii. Locations adjacent to buildings, internal drive aisles, or landscape terminal islands;
iv. Front Yard. Level 1 and Level 2 EV charging stations may be located within front yard parking areas subject to the following:
1. The charging equipment is integrated into a standard parking row and does not create a standalone facility;
2. No canopy structures are provided;
3. Equipment height does not exceed 5 feet;
4. The number of EV spaces shall not exceed 10 percent of the total parking along the frontage; and
5. The installation is visually subordinate to the site, including compliance with landscaping or screening standards.
2. High Visibility Frontage Limitation.
i. No more than 25 percent of EV charging spaces along a single street frontage shall be located within the first parking bay directly abutting a public street classified as an arterial, collector, or other corridor as determined by the City Council.
3. Site Triangle Considerations.
i. Level 1 and Level 2 may be located within designated vision sight triangle provided equipment height does not exceed 5 feet and is visually subordinate to adjacent landscaping or structures.
B. Level 3 (including support facilities, equipment and the like).
Due to their increased scale and visibility, Level 3 are subject to the following additional standards:
1. Permitted Locations.
i. Rear parking areas;
ii. Side parking areas screened from public streets;
iii. Interior parking fields not visible from a public right of way.
2. Prohibited Locations.
i. Within required front setbacks;
ii. Between the primary building façade and a public street, except in side parking areas as referenced in 1009.1-10.C.2.II.
iii. Within required vision sight triangles.
iv. Adjacent High Traffic Corridor Standards. Along roadways classified as:
1. Principal arterials;
2. State routes;
3. Other corridors designated by City Council;
3. Setbacks. Level 3 and associated Electric Vehicle Infrastructure shall be;
1. Setback a minimum of 30 feet from the right of way; or
2. Visually screened per the requirements of Section 50-53 Landscape Strip Planting Requirements.
4. Design Standards.
i. Maximum height. EV Charging stations and associated structures shall be a maximum of 15 feet, unless otherwise permitted by the Community Development Director or their designee.
ii. Canopy roofs shall utilize:
1. Flat or low-profile designs; and
2. Non reflective materials to reduce glare.
3. Lighting integrated into EV canopies shall:
a. Be fully screened;
b. Oriented downward; and
c. Comply with applicable lighting standards.

